       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient's weight, kidney function, liver function and allergy status don't change that limit. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures and GI or bleeding effects, and the dose is well past the range where more drug adds benefit.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n\n1. **Enter 200 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual maximum. Titration normally starts at 50 mg daily and goes up in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of a week or more.\n2. **Enter a different dose.** If you meant a different amount, such as 40 mg or 100 mg, give me the dose.\n3. **Enter 400 mg as written.** If it's intentional, for example a specialist-directed regimen, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying the above-maximum dose was verified. You may also want to add monitoring, such as an ECG and a check for interacting drugs."
      }
